// mecatl driver API: the remote learning-attempt repository protocol.
//
// This transport carries only the bounded, content-free learning domain record:
// opaque partitions, identifiers, versions and digests; closed lifecycle values;
// generations; timestamps; and proposal/skill links. It never carries prompts,
// transcript/event content, paths, principals, credentials, headers, diagnostics,
// or backend error text. AttemptErrorDetail is the closed safe error vocabulary.
// Caller ownership enforcement and caller-facing RPC separation are added by the
// application boundary; this service is the infrastructure repository seam.
// ADR-0250 watches session events only: this protocol has no attempt watch,
// cursor, process-local substitute, or watch envelope. Advisory attempt
// notifications require a separately specified durable attempt-change-feed ADR.

